  "rationale": "Late Ellington's greatest extended suite and one of the canon's clearest consensus records: Penguin Guide Core Collection at its maximum rating, DownBeat 5 stars (Dan Morgenstern: 'a great record, and by any standard one of the major musical events of 1971'), and the 1971 Grammy for Best Jazz Performance by a Big Band. It also carries an unusual kind of session gravity: these are Johnny Hodges's final recordings — he died between the two sessions — and Paul Gonsalves's Portrait of Sidney Bechet answers him. Lineage is direct: it extends the suite form already in this canon through Such Sweet Thunder and The Far East Suite, and it is the record that shows the 1970 band, with Norris Turney and Wild Bill Davis aboard, still composing at the level of the 1940s band. It still plays: the portraits work as music, not as a history lesson.",
