    "case_for": "The dossier reports Penguin Guide Core Collection recognition, a five-star DownBeat review by Dan Morgenstern, and a Grammy win: substantial convergence across independent evaluative traditions, although the critical citations need tighter source attribution. The suite extends the orchestral lineage of Such Sweet Thunder and The Far East Suite through distinctive blues, gospel, second-line rhythms, and instrumental portraits rather than merely repeating their achievement. Johnny Hodges's final recordings give it exceptional session gravity, supported by the personnel and session documentation (S1–S3). Wild Bill Davis's organ on \"Blues for New Orleans\" and the ensemble drive of \"Second Line\" make its historical argument immediately accessible as music.",
